{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Ring.Defs"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.seed_not_determined_of_depthTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.seed_not_determined_of_depthTwo","kind":"theorem","line":106,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.lean#L106-L115","doc":"**Depth-2 horn.** For *every* kernel `(p, s)`, and any two prescribed values,\nthere are two solutions of the depth-2 relation agreeing on the forced one-body\nseed and disagreeing at `w_3`. The relation therefore does not determine `w_3`:\nthe double cover reparametrises the unknown rather than removing it, exactly as\n`kernel_coeff_existsUnique` records for the uncovered case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.twoStep_isDepthTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.twoStep_isDepthTwo","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.lean#L103-L104","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.twoStep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.twoStep","kind":"def","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.lean#L96-L101","doc":"The solution of a depth-2 relation from its two seeds. Used to witness that\nthe second seed is genuinely free. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.not_depthOne_of_w3_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.not_depthOne_of_w3_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.lean#L90-L94","doc":"Contrapositive, in the form the measurement meets it: a nonzero `w_3` rules\nout every depth-1 kernel on the odd branch at once. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.w3_eq_zero_of_depthOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.w3_eq_zero_of_depthOne","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.lean#L83-L88","doc":"The consequence for the unknown: `w_3 = v 1 = 0`, for every kernel `r`. So a\ndepth-1 kernel on the cover predicts a vanishing connected three-body cumulant,\nwhich the AME2020 inversion (`b₃ = +1.426222` MeV) contradicts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.oddBranch_eq_zero_of_depthOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.oddBranch_eq_zero_of_depthOne","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.lean#L74-L81","doc":"**Depth-1 horn.** The one-body weight is the binding of a single free\nnucleon, hence zero; a depth-1 kernel propagates that to the whole odd branch. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.DepthTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.DepthTwo","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.lean#L71-L72","doc":"A **depth-2** scalar kernel on the double cover. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.DepthOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.DepthOne","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DoubleCoverOddBranchSeed.lean#L67-L69","doc":"The odd body-order branch of the weights, reindexed: `v k = w (2k+1)`. A\n**depth-1** scalar kernel on the double cover relates consecutive half-shifts. ","signatureChunk":0}]}